Only 4% of priests have a cloak of magic resistance, so I think the odds
that the High Priest can be taken out with a wand of death compare
favourably to the odds that you have a helm of opposite alignment and
hence can zap all the Riders you need face. Indeed, the High Priest
doesn't have the annoying habit of coming back to life, so you don't run
nearly so high a risk of running out of zaps and having to fight him
anyway.

>At the Sanctum it's
>different; mostly I have no straight line to target the priest from afar,

I don't see the difficulty of lining up the priest for a volley of daggers
as appreciably greater or less than the difficulty of getting a clear line
of fire to a Rider in the press of the Astral Plane.

>There's no such thing as a well defined "ascension-ready"-ness.

The presence of grey areas does not mean there are not black and white
areas.

>>... and we haven't even talked about how going onto the Plane of Air
>>Burdened with 150HP will end up.
